              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.349,
            0.846,
            0.406
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "["
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Show that triangles ∆ADB and ∆ADC can be made into halves of a rectangle. Figure out how they should be assembled to get a rectangle. Use cut-outs if necessary.]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.415,
            0.845,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. [Śulba-Sūtras] Give a method to convert a rectangle into an isosceles triangle by dissection."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.463,
            0.847,
            0.54
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. Which has greater area — an equilateral triangle or a square of the same sidelength as the triangle? Which has greater area — two identical equilateral triangles together or a square of the same sidelength as the triangle? Give reasons."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.558,
            0.273,
            0.579
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Rhombus"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.59,
            0.848,
            0.683
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since a rhombus is a parallelogram, the area formula for a parallelogram holds for a rhombus as well. However, the additional properties of a rhombus give us another method to transform a rhombus into a rectangle of the same area by dissection. This method occurs in one of the Śulba-Sūtras."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.693,
            0.364,
            0.716
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Try working this out!"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
